WEBVTT

00:01:21.733 --> 00:01:25.824
&lt;i&gt;Captain's log, stardate 58053.9.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:25.867 --> 00:01:28.479
&lt;i&gt;The&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos &lt;i&gt;is escorting
a Doopler emissary&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:28.522 --> 00:01:31.612
&lt;i&gt;to Starbase 25
for trade negotiations.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:31.656 --> 00:01:34.920
&lt;i&gt;Dooplers are a species
which involuntarily duplicate&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:34.963 --> 00:01:37.183
&lt;i&gt;as an emotional
defense mechanism.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:37.227 --> 00:01:40.143
&lt;i&gt;We've been walking on eggshells
the entire trip.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:40.186 --> 00:01:42.797
Emissary, the last few days with
you

00:01:42.841 --> 00:01:45.148
have been very... careful.

00:01:45.191 --> 00:01:48.281
Your hospitality is appreciated,
Captain, as are your efforts

00:01:48.325 --> 00:01:50.283
to prevent me
from dooplercating.

00:01:55.593 --> 00:01:58.422
- Oh!

00:01:58.465 --> 00:02:00.119
Uh, excuse me.

00:02:00.163 --> 00:02:02.774
I must ready
for arrival to the station.

00:02:06.517 --> 00:02:08.432
This has been the most stressful
week of my life.

00:02:08.475 --> 00:02:10.216
How did we get on Doopler duty?

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:11.696
Well, it's all worth it.

00:02:11.739 --> 00:02:13.741
We'll get to Starbase 25

00:02:13.785 --> 00:02:16.309
just in time
for the Command Conference.

00:02:16.353 --> 00:02:18.398
Is that the one
with the epic after-party?

00:02:18.442 --> 00:02:20.226
Oh, yeah. Three years ago,

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:22.837
Admiral Slattery got so drunk,
he commandeered a light cruiser.

00:02:22.881 --> 00:02:26.189
He didn't sober up till he was
halfway to the Delta Quadrant.

00:02:26.232 --> 00:02:29.496
I'll be the only
California-class captain there

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:30.845
because of my heroics

00:02:30.889 --> 00:02:32.499
in the battle
against the Pakleds.

00:02:32.543 --> 00:02:36.677
Soon Doopler duty
will be a thing of the past.

00:02:38.201 --> 00:02:39.724
Uh, sometimes this job
feels like

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:41.726
it's just stacking crates
in storage bays.

00:02:41.769 --> 00:02:43.336
- What are we doing next?
- Crate stacking.

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:45.164
- Storage Bay Seven.
- I can't believe

00:02:45.208 --> 00:02:46.513
we're going to be docked
right outside

00:02:46.557 --> 00:02:47.906
the wildest party in Starfleet,

00:02:47.949 --> 00:02:49.690
but instead of getting torn,
we'll be stacking.

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:51.910
I could be hanging out
with so many captains

00:02:51.953 --> 00:02:53.694
who are looking
for their next number one.

00:02:53.738 --> 00:02:55.479
- I bet right now

00:02:55.522 --> 00:02:57.481
- you wish
you were still on the &lt;i&gt;Titan.
- It was amazing.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:57.524 --> 00:02:59.570
I swear the replicated water
just tasted better.

00:02:59.613 --> 00:03:00.962
And don't even get me started

00:03:01.006 --> 00:03:02.399
on how soft
the bridge chairs were.

00:03:02.442 --> 00:03:03.704
- Ooh! And the holodecks...
- Okay.

00:03:03.748 --> 00:03:05.315
I wasn't looking
for the sales pitch.

00:03:05.358 --> 00:03:07.099
I meant if you were still
on a capital ship like that,

00:03:07.142 --> 00:03:08.883
you'd be guaranteed an invite
to this party.

00:03:08.927 --> 00:03:11.973
Yeah, my stupid transporter
clone William is probably going.

00:03:12.017 --> 00:03:14.149
You haven't even met him,
but trust me, he's so annoying.

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:16.021
Real stickler for the rules,
kind of a butt kisser.

00:03:16.064 --> 00:03:18.241
Wait, wait, shut up, shut up.
The &lt;i&gt;Titan's&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:18.284 --> 00:03:20.199
on the other side of the system
deterring the Pakleds.

00:03:20.243 --> 00:03:21.635
So?

00:03:21.679 --> 00:03:23.985
So there's no way
they can make it here in time.

00:03:24.029 --> 00:03:26.118
William's invite
is just sitting there.

00:03:26.161 --> 00:03:28.555
You can pose as your clone,
and I can be your plus-one.

00:03:28.599 --> 00:03:30.514
You're right.
Just to be safe, I'll call

00:03:30.557 --> 00:03:32.559
clone Boimler and make sure
he's cool with it. Aah!

00:03:32.603 --> 00:03:35.345
- Are you crazy?
- You're right.
I now realize that was crazy.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:44.310
After a hard day
of working on the ship,

00:03:44.354 --> 00:03:47.139
nothing relaxes me like building
a smaller version of the ship.

00:03:47.182 --> 00:03:49.924
Now we just have to get the
tiny deflector shields on line.

00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:51.274
Boy, before I lost my memory,

00:03:51.317 --> 00:03:53.014
I did some great work
on this thing.

00:03:53.058 --> 00:03:55.843
- Look at those phase inverters.
- I like mini Mariner

00:03:55.887 --> 00:03:58.150
bossing around tiny Boimler
in the itty-bitty bar.

00:03:58.193 --> 00:04:00.544
Huh, there's something etched
onto the side of the manifold.

00:04:00.587 --> 00:04:01.980
Looks like old me
left some directions

00:04:02.023 --> 00:04:03.242
on how to get
the shields working.

00:04:03.286 --> 00:04:06.724
"Field distortion amplifier 88."

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:08.900
And then there's
three squiggly lines.

00:04:08.943 --> 00:04:10.380
What does that mean?

00:04:10.423 --> 00:04:12.817
I don't know.
But if I did it once,

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:14.166
I can do it again.

00:04:14.209 --> 00:04:15.820
Aah!
- Oh, sorry!

00:04:20.912 --> 00:04:23.697
&lt;i&gt;Ah, Captain Freeman.
I guess this means&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:23.741 --> 00:04:26.091
&lt;i&gt;you've had a good trip
with your Doopler guest.&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:26.134 --> 00:04:28.223
- It was exhausting.

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:31.357
Between us, I can't get him
off the ship fast enough.

00:04:31.401 --> 00:04:33.925
- Um...
- The man is
so emotionally fragile.

00:04:33.968 --> 00:04:35.187
Fragile?

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:37.276
Was I too much trouble?

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:39.104
No, no, no, no, no,
you were great.

00:04:39.147 --> 00:04:40.758
I love having you here.

00:04:40.801 --> 00:04:43.630
I was a bad guest. I'm so, so...

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:47.591
- Oh, no.
- I dooplercated!

00:04:47.634 --> 00:04:49.375
This is so embarrassing.

00:04:49.419 --> 00:04:51.029
No, it's-it's fine.

00:04:51.072 --> 00:04:54.119
Nothing is more mortifying
than dooplercating.

00:04:54.162 --> 00:04:55.947
We both did it.

00:04:57.514 --> 00:05:00.343
- Oh, he just dooplercated.
- Don't look at me!

00:05:00.386 --> 00:05:03.607
Stop! It's fine.
You are all great.

00:05:05.783 --> 00:05:07.175
&lt;i&gt;Freeman,
I can't risk this station&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:07.219 --> 00:05:08.786
&lt;i&gt;being overrun with Dooplers.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:08.829 --> 00:05:10.353
&lt;i&gt;The&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos &lt;i&gt;
won't be allowed to dock&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:10.396 --> 00:05:11.484
&lt;i&gt;until you sort this out.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:11.528 --> 00:05:13.312
We aren't allowed
on the station?!

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.926
Oh, yeah.
Looking sassy. Yeah.

00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:20.319
Should we be in skants for this?

00:05:20.363 --> 00:05:21.799
Nobody wears those anymore.
Don't overthink it.

00:05:21.842 --> 00:05:23.801
Right, but maybe we could take
our skants in a bag

00:05:23.844 --> 00:05:25.455
just in case we get there
and everyone's in a skant?

00:05:25.498 --> 00:05:26.978
&lt;i&gt;Attention, all decks.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:27.021 --> 00:05:29.328
&lt;i&gt;The Dooplers
are exponentially duplicating,&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:29.372 --> 00:05:32.636
&lt;i&gt;which is
a totally cool thing to do.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:32.679 --> 00:05:35.639
&lt;i&gt;If you see a Doopler,
just smile and look away.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:35.682 --> 00:05:37.902
&lt;i&gt;You're telling the whole ship
about us?!&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:39.991 --> 00:05:41.384
Does that mean we're not going?

00:05:41.427 --> 00:05:43.124
It means we're &lt;i&gt;definitely&lt;/i&gt; going.

00:05:43.168 --> 00:05:44.952
Chaos on the bridge
means no one's gonna notice

00:05:44.996 --> 00:05:46.954
one little transporter override.
Come on.

00:05:46.998 --> 00:05:48.565
Ooh!

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:55.528
Whoa, I've never been
on a station this old.

00:05:55.572 --> 00:05:56.877
It's like a whole city.

00:05:56.921 --> 00:05:58.052
Yeah, it's great,
but it kind of smells

00:05:58.096 --> 00:05:59.271
like pee sometimes.

00:05:59.314 --> 00:06:00.446
Come on,
we got to find the party.

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:02.143
The location's always secret.

00:06:02.187 --> 00:06:04.363
This place is massive.
How are we gonna find anything?

00:06:04.407 --> 00:06:05.669
Follow me. I used to live here.

00:06:05.712 --> 00:06:07.671
Of course you did.

00:06:07.714 --> 00:06:09.150
Ooh, they've got a Quark's now.

00:06:09.194 --> 00:06:10.587
That used to just be
an empty lot

00:06:10.630 --> 00:06:12.589
where teens would make mistakes.

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:15.635
Remember Becky Mariner?

00:06:15.679 --> 00:06:16.636
She's back.

00:06:26.603 --> 00:06:28.648
What are you doing?
We don't have time to shop.

00:06:28.692 --> 00:06:30.563
Hmm.

00:06:30.607 --> 00:06:32.957
You dare set foot
on this station

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.785
after what you did to me, Becky?

00:06:34.828 --> 00:06:37.265
-"Becky"?
- Oh, get over it, Malvus.

00:06:37.309 --> 00:06:40.007
I should disintegrate you for
stranding me on Ceti Alpha IV,

00:06:40.051 --> 00:06:42.793
which I'll have you know
is much worse than Ceti Alpha V.

00:06:42.836 --> 00:06:44.098
I don't strand people.

00:06:44.142 --> 00:06:45.839
She stranded me on Rubicon III.

00:06:45.883 --> 00:06:48.015
- You stranded yourself.
What about on Axilus?

00:06:48.059 --> 00:06:50.278
O-Okay, yeah,
I stranded you there.

00:06:50.322 --> 00:06:51.454
Your boyfriend has it right.

00:06:51.497 --> 00:06:53.020
- Ugh.
- Not my boyfriend.

00:06:53.064 --> 00:06:54.413
Ah, it's nice to meet someone
who understands

00:06:54.457 --> 00:06:56.067
how hard it is working with her.

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:57.547
And the same to you.

00:06:57.590 --> 00:06:59.287
All right, I'm sorry
I left you on Ceti Alpha.

00:06:59.331 --> 00:07:00.811
I really thought
there was life there.

00:07:00.854 --> 00:07:02.334
Listen,
we could really use your help...

00:07:02.377 --> 00:07:04.989
that stupid Starfleet party.

00:07:05.032 --> 00:07:07.339
- You have to know where it is.
- Of course I do.

00:07:07.382 --> 00:07:09.515
And I'd be happy to share it
if you help me move

00:07:09.559 --> 00:07:11.517
some merchandise to storage.

00:07:11.561 --> 00:07:14.172
- Aw, crates.
- Wait, hold on. What's in them?

00:07:14.215 --> 00:07:18.698
Limited edition
Commander Data bubble bath.

00:07:18.742 --> 00:07:21.832
- You sure this isn't a Lore?
- Meh, a couple might be Lores.

00:07:21.875 --> 00:07:23.573
Hmm.

00:07:23.616 --> 00:07:26.184
- Oh! Watch out!
Hot, hot, hot, hot.

00:07:26.227 --> 00:07:28.273
The engines work, but no lights.

00:07:28.316 --> 00:07:29.883
What am I doing wrong?

00:07:29.927 --> 00:07:31.406
Oh, hey, another message
from last-year me.

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.887
"Shield emitters equal sign

00:07:33.931 --> 00:07:35.933
- squiggly line"?
- All right, clear out.

00:07:35.976 --> 00:07:38.588
- This area is being used
for emergency Doopler holding.

00:07:38.631 --> 00:07:39.937
There's so many of me.

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:41.634
Hey, careful.

00:07:41.678 --> 00:07:44.332
Oh, no, I bumped your toy!

00:07:44.376 --> 00:07:45.899
We need to find somewhere
to finish the model.

00:07:45.943 --> 00:07:48.075
You're leaving because of me.

00:07:48.119 --> 00:07:49.555
Yeah. I mean, it's pretty clear.

00:07:52.384 --> 00:07:54.604
There's no need
to feel embarrassed.

00:07:54.647 --> 00:07:56.083
Thank you. You're very kind.

00:07:56.127 --> 00:07:58.129
Wait! That's what someone says

00:07:58.172 --> 00:08:01.001
- when there &lt;i&gt;is&lt;/i&gt; a reason
to be embarrassed!

00:08:01.045 --> 00:08:02.176
Okay,

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:03.961
I'm just not gonna say anything.

00:08:04.004 --> 00:08:06.529
We can just be silent.

00:08:08.052 --> 00:08:10.445
She's giving us
the silent treatment!

00:08:10.489 --> 00:08:11.969
- That's even worse!

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:15.712
This should fix
the harmonic... Ow!

00:08:15.755 --> 00:08:18.410
Who rerouted power
through the harmonic dampeners?

00:08:18.453 --> 00:08:20.281
- I guess you did?
- Ow.

00:08:20.325 --> 00:08:21.979
Stupid me.

00:08:22.022 --> 00:08:24.503
- Maybe we just put it away.
- No, I have to finish this.

00:08:27.158 --> 00:08:28.725
Excuse us. Sorry. Ow!

00:08:28.768 --> 00:08:31.989
- Excuse me!
- Oh, no! We're in the way!

00:08:32.032 --> 00:08:33.643
- Run!

00:08:35.427 --> 00:08:37.081
Aw, sugar.

00:08:38.865 --> 00:08:41.041
Hey, we could bring one of these
into the party

00:08:41.085 --> 00:08:42.913
and be like,
"Anybody order bottle service?"

00:08:42.956 --> 00:08:45.568
You know what? You didn't have
to tell Malvus I abandoned you.

00:08:45.611 --> 00:08:47.657
- It was an accident.
- We were just having fun.

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:50.573
I wasn't. That was a private
thing between you and me.

00:08:50.616 --> 00:08:52.792
You're always telling people
embarrassing stories about &lt;i&gt;me.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:52.836 --> 00:08:55.142
That's different.
My stories are hilarious.

00:08:55.186 --> 00:08:57.405
- And you're the one
that abandoned me.
- What?

00:08:57.449 --> 00:08:59.625
- Ooh, crap, crap, crap.

00:08:59.669 --> 00:09:01.279
Oh, it's security.
They're pulling us over.

00:09:01.322 --> 00:09:02.976
- Aah!
We're not supposed to be here!
- Shut up.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:04.848
- Just stay calm.
- Yeah. Yeah. Uh...

00:09:04.891 --> 00:09:06.850
Yeah. Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

00:09:06.893 --> 00:09:08.634
We just got stopped by security.

00:09:08.678 --> 00:09:11.071
&lt;i&gt;They're always amped up
on party day.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:11.115 --> 00:09:12.464
Yeah, for a moment
I was worried

00:09:12.507 --> 00:09:13.813
this was a stolen kart
or something.

00:09:13.857 --> 00:09:15.293
&lt;i&gt;It's not,
but the illegal weapons&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:15.336 --> 00:09:16.599
&lt;i&gt;under the bubble bath are.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:17.643 --> 00:09:19.645
Klingon disruptors.

00:09:19.689 --> 00:09:20.690
Malvus!

00:09:20.733 --> 00:09:22.430
&lt;i&gt;Enjoy the penal colony.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:25.433 --> 00:09:27.740
Let's just explain
that we were tricked

00:09:27.784 --> 00:09:29.786
into carrying illegal cargo
by your criminal friend.

00:09:29.829 --> 00:09:32.310
No, station security has a rep
for being crooked.

00:09:32.353 --> 00:09:33.920
They aren't gonna let us off
with a warning

00:09:33.964 --> 00:09:35.139
and a glass of Thai iced tea.

00:09:35.182 --> 00:09:36.662
They'll coerce a confession,

00:09:36.706 --> 00:09:38.142
then sell our combadges
on the black market.

00:09:38.185 --> 00:09:40.100
Lucky for us,
they're terrible drivers.

00:09:40.144 --> 00:09:41.928
Why is that lucky?

00:09:49.936 --> 00:09:51.372
- Dabo!

00:09:51.416 --> 00:09:53.679
Casino!

00:09:53.723 --> 00:09:56.639
- Barbershop!

00:09:56.682 --> 00:09:59.250
Fine men's clothing!

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:15.832
Get out... What?

00:10:15.875 --> 00:10:16.963
Hey!

00:10:24.710 --> 00:10:26.059
Backwards time.

00:10:39.377 --> 00:10:41.509
Whoa!

00:10:41.553 --> 00:10:43.120
Fish people!

00:10:43.163 --> 00:10:45.731
- Sorry!
- Hey, we're not people!

00:10:48.429 --> 00:10:50.910
Don't go down the stairs!

00:10:50.954 --> 00:10:53.478
Dude, I would never go
down the stairs.

00:11:05.142 --> 00:11:07.448
Vulcans! Vulcans! Vulcans!

00:11:09.276 --> 00:11:11.539
Fascinating.

00:11:11.583 --> 00:11:12.932
- I can't take it anymore.
- Hey! Hey!

00:11:12.976 --> 00:11:14.673
I got a model here. Stay back!

00:11:14.717 --> 00:11:16.370
This is humiliating.

00:11:18.242 --> 00:11:20.723
We got to get to higher ground.

00:11:21.854 --> 00:11:24.291
Oh!

00:11:24.335 --> 00:11:26.859
- Forget the model!
Are you crazy?!
Got it!

00:11:28.905 --> 00:11:31.255
We can escape
through the maintenance hatch.

00:11:31.298 --> 00:11:33.431
It was sealed off months ago.
Don't you remember?

00:11:33.474 --> 00:11:36.260
No, Tendi, I don't remember.
And that's the problem.

00:11:36.303 --> 00:11:38.479
My whole deal
is repairing starships.

00:11:38.523 --> 00:11:40.264
If I can't fix this little toy,

00:11:40.307 --> 00:11:42.179
then I don't even know
who I am anymore.

00:11:42.222 --> 00:11:44.572
- You're still
Samanthan Rutherford.
- Am I?

00:11:44.616 --> 00:11:47.619
The old me was better.
I can't figure out his notes,

00:11:47.662 --> 00:11:49.664
and I'm, like, a year behind
being friends with you.

00:11:49.708 --> 00:11:51.536
It's like I'm competing
with my own ghost.

00:12:00.632 --> 00:12:02.503
Cool, the aviary.

00:12:02.547 --> 00:12:04.767
- I went on a date here once.
- Avians!

00:12:05.724 --> 00:12:07.813
- Oh, God! Oh, God!
No, no, no, no!

00:12:20.913 --> 00:12:23.960
Oh, yeah. "Let's move
to the aviary," he says.

00:12:24.003 --> 00:12:27.485
"It'll be so quiet," he says.

00:12:27.528 --> 00:12:30.009
Ha! We lost 'em. Never doubt me.

00:12:32.229 --> 00:12:34.187
This is how I die.

00:12:47.810 --> 00:12:50.290
Still alive.

00:12:59.604 --> 00:13:02.172
I barfed up bubble bath.

00:13:02.215 --> 00:13:04.391
Yeah, I was there.
Thank you for the update.

00:13:04.435 --> 00:13:07.438
We can forget about
the party, because guess what.

00:13:07.481 --> 00:13:08.918
We're probably
getting arrested instead.

00:13:08.961 --> 00:13:11.268
No way. I didn't
put on underwear for nothing.

00:13:11.311 --> 00:13:13.270
&lt;i&gt;Mariner.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:13.313 --> 00:13:15.794
&lt;i&gt;Thank the gods whom I worship
that you're alive.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:15.838 --> 00:13:17.927
Shut up. If you don't tell me
where that party is,

00:13:17.970 --> 00:13:20.930
I'm telling security I know
who those disruptors belong to.

00:13:20.973 --> 00:13:22.496
&lt;i&gt;But you would get arrested, too.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:24.672
Yeah, and then we'd both be
in the same cell.

00:13:24.716 --> 00:13:27.153
- Just you and me. &lt;i&gt;
- All right, all right.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:27.197 --> 00:13:29.677
&lt;i&gt;I'll send you the location.
But you still owe me.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:29.721 --> 00:13:31.418
I owe a foot up your ass.

00:13:31.462 --> 00:13:34.378
Ballroom Alpha? Aw, that's
where all the big parties are.

00:13:34.421 --> 00:13:36.728
- How is that even a secret?

00:13:38.208 --> 00:13:40.906
I knew we should have brought
the skants.

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:47.478
This is stupid.
We're soaking wet.

00:13:47.521 --> 00:13:48.914
Shh, shh, shh,
there's the bouncer.

00:13:48.958 --> 00:13:50.089
Name?

00:13:50.133 --> 00:13:51.482
Brad... &lt;i&gt;William.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:51.525 --> 00:13:53.440
Boimler. USS &lt;i&gt;Titan.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:53.484 --> 00:13:54.789
Go on in.

00:13:54.833 --> 00:13:56.400
- It worked!
- Yeah, he just...

00:13:56.443 --> 00:13:58.184
he loves being on lists.

00:13:58.228 --> 00:13:59.403
Very excited. Whoa!

00:13:59.446 --> 00:14:01.013
- Not you.
- This is Beckett Mariner.

00:14:01.057 --> 00:14:02.928
- She's my plus-one.
- What ship you on?

00:14:02.972 --> 00:14:04.974
- Uh, the &lt;i&gt;Voyager-D.
- Mm.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:05.017 --> 00:14:07.367
Beckett Mariner,
ensign on the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:07.411 --> 00:14:10.066
Nope, sorry.
Luna-class and above only.

00:14:10.109 --> 00:14:11.981
They're not letting me in.

00:14:12.024 --> 00:14:14.200
Whatever. There's, like,
a million other things to do

00:14:14.244 --> 00:14:16.724
- on a station this big.
- But this is the best thing,

00:14:16.768 --> 00:14:17.943
- right?
- Fine.

00:14:17.987 --> 00:14:19.118
Just go in without me.

00:14:19.162 --> 00:14:20.424
I'm not gonna abandon you
out here.

00:14:20.467 --> 00:14:22.208
Oh, please. You love abandoning.

00:14:22.252 --> 00:14:23.818
No, I don't. &lt;i&gt;
You're&lt;/i&gt; the abandoner.

00:14:23.862 --> 00:14:24.950
You didn't think twice
about taking

00:14:24.994 --> 00:14:26.299
that promotion to the &lt;i&gt;Titan.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:26.343 --> 00:14:27.474
You just couldn't wait
to leave me,

00:14:27.518 --> 00:14:29.085
just like everybody else.

00:14:29.128 --> 00:14:30.434
You're still mad
about the &lt;i&gt;Titan?&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:30.477 --> 00:14:31.783
Why didn't you
bring it up before?

00:14:31.826 --> 00:14:33.089
Of course I'm still mad!
I've been waiting

00:14:33.132 --> 00:14:34.873
for you to apologize for weeks,
you dumb jerk.

00:14:34.917 --> 00:14:36.135
How was I supposed to know that?

00:14:36.179 --> 00:14:38.007
Maybe try being honest sometime.

00:14:38.050 --> 00:14:40.052
Whatever.
I earned that promotion,

00:14:40.096 --> 00:14:42.185
but I guess you have
to make it all about you.

00:14:42.228 --> 00:14:44.100
- Some friend.

00:14:45.101 --> 00:14:47.277
Hey.
It's tough being vulnerable.

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.192
Believe me, I know.

00:14:49.235 --> 00:14:51.194
Yeah... shut up.

00:14:51.237 --> 00:14:53.587
- Whoa.

00:14:59.724 --> 00:15:00.986
Whoa!

00:15:01.030 --> 00:15:02.683
Captain Shelby
and her number one.

00:15:03.815 --> 00:15:05.164
Captain Exley
and his number one.

00:15:05.208 --> 00:15:06.992
Hey, you made it.

00:15:07.036 --> 00:15:09.516
I haven't seen you
since Centauri IV.

00:15:14.565 --> 00:15:16.132
This is so awkward!

00:15:16.175 --> 00:15:17.960
You're telling me!

00:15:18.003 --> 00:15:19.744
I'm sorry
I can't finish the model.

00:15:19.787 --> 00:15:21.180
I just have to get used
to knowing

00:15:21.224 --> 00:15:22.834
that the old me
was a better engineer.

00:15:22.877 --> 00:15:25.141
What? Rutherford,
you have it all wrong.

00:15:25.184 --> 00:15:27.491
- Old you
never finished it, either.
- What do you mean?

00:15:27.534 --> 00:15:28.622
We always stopped
at the warp core,

00:15:28.666 --> 00:15:30.885
- and then we'd start over again.
- Why?

00:15:30.929 --> 00:15:33.236
Because as long as we
were working on this,

00:15:33.279 --> 00:15:34.628
people left us alone.

00:15:34.672 --> 00:15:36.195
It was like
our social deflector dish.

00:15:36.239 --> 00:15:38.632
We got to hang out
without anyone bugging us.

00:15:38.676 --> 00:15:40.547
So all these notes
from old me...?

00:15:40.591 --> 00:15:43.028
Are probably just to slow down
and buy time.

00:15:43.072 --> 00:15:44.377
I &lt;i&gt;wasn't&lt;/i&gt; smarter than me!

00:15:44.421 --> 00:15:46.075
- I'm glad you're feeling better.

00:15:46.118 --> 00:15:47.424
Too bad we're gonna get crushed.

00:15:47.467 --> 00:15:49.730
Not if we detonate
the warp core.

00:15:53.865 --> 00:15:56.476
- Come on.

00:15:58.391 --> 00:16:01.351
&lt;i&gt;-Ejecting warp core&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:01.394 --> 00:16:05.485
&lt;i&gt;in five, four, three, two...&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:05.529 --> 00:16:07.922
Hot, hot, hot, hot.

00:16:15.539 --> 00:16:17.541
Uh... Whoa!

00:16:19.064 --> 00:16:20.935
Is this because of us?

00:16:20.979 --> 00:16:23.068
They don't like us!

00:16:26.332 --> 00:16:28.900
Uh, can I get
five more of these?

00:16:28.943 --> 00:16:31.511
- You, uh, think
that's a good idea?
- Hmm.

00:16:31.555 --> 00:16:33.818
Interesting. I'm actually going
for "bad idea."

00:16:33.861 --> 00:16:35.472
- Put those on my tab.

00:16:35.515 --> 00:16:37.604
Plus a prune juice spritz.

00:16:39.128 --> 00:16:41.086
Don't tell me
the party was boring.

00:16:41.130 --> 00:16:43.262
It was amazing. Nonstop sliders.

00:16:43.306 --> 00:16:46.526
You love sliders.
So why'd you leave?

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:48.006
- It just wasn't fun.
- Hmm.

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:49.747
- Not enough famous admirals?
- There were,

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:52.097
but you weren't there
to make fun of them with me.

00:16:52.141 --> 00:16:55.100
I'm sorry I left
for the &lt;i&gt;Titan&lt;/i&gt; the way I did.

00:16:55.144 --> 00:16:58.147
I guess I was worried
you would talk me out of it.

00:16:58.190 --> 00:16:59.713
I didn't mean
to hurt your feelings.

00:16:59.757 --> 00:17:02.151
I didn't even know
you &lt;i&gt;had&lt;/i&gt; feelings.

00:17:02.194 --> 00:17:03.413
Of course I do.

00:17:03.456 --> 00:17:05.197
I just don't show them
to everyone.

00:17:05.241 --> 00:17:07.330
I don't know why
I make an exception for you.

00:17:07.373 --> 00:17:09.462
Maybe because
you're my number one.

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:13.727
Wow. No, if anything,
you're &lt;i&gt;my&lt;/i&gt; number one.

00:17:13.771 --> 00:17:15.555
- I'm your mentor.
Nice try.

00:17:15.599 --> 00:17:18.036
- We've already done that.
- It goes by force
of personality.

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:19.429
Me. Then you.

00:17:19.472 --> 00:17:22.432
No, don't make me
bump you down to number two.

00:17:22.475 --> 00:17:25.261
Thanks for coming to hang.
I'm sorry I ruined the party.

00:17:25.304 --> 00:17:27.872
I can replicate sliders whenever
I want back on the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:27.915 --> 00:17:29.308
Who needs to be at the coolest,

00:17:29.352 --> 00:17:31.441
most prestigious party
of the year?

00:17:36.098 --> 00:17:38.883
I'm sorry, Captain!
The crowd has me now.

00:17:38.926 --> 00:17:40.928
Oh, no!

00:17:40.972 --> 00:17:42.887
Enough. Enough!

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:45.455
Stop being
such whiny little [bleep]!

00:17:45.498 --> 00:17:47.239
Wh-What did you say?

00:17:47.283 --> 00:17:51.591
You idiots need to shut up
and stop being sniveling babies!

00:17:53.463 --> 00:17:55.508
Did you see that?
I berated them,

00:17:55.552 --> 00:17:57.119
and they recombined.

00:17:57.162 --> 00:17:59.164
Getting embarrassed
makes them lose control,

00:17:59.208 --> 00:18:01.035
but getting pissed
helps them get it back.

00:18:01.079 --> 00:18:02.428
Hey! You're a jerk!

00:18:02.472 --> 00:18:05.039
Excuse me?

00:18:05.083 --> 00:18:06.867
Attention, everyone.

00:18:06.911 --> 00:18:09.348
&lt;i&gt;Stop being careful
around the Dooplers.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:09.392 --> 00:18:12.308
&lt;i&gt;Yell at them.
Call them spineless punks.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:12.351 --> 00:18:13.961
&lt;i&gt;I know we're Starfleet,&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:14.005 --> 00:18:17.530
&lt;i&gt;but really give them
a piece of your mind.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:17.574 --> 00:18:19.967
Your pagh is weak,
and it disgusts me!

00:18:20.011 --> 00:18:23.362
I don't even know what that is,
but I don't like your tone.

00:18:25.930 --> 00:18:27.018
This is Engineering.

00:18:27.061 --> 00:18:28.280
You're in my house now!

00:18:28.324 --> 00:18:30.500
You wouldn't know
a reecon converter

00:18:30.543 --> 00:18:32.284
from a tulox shifter!

00:18:32.328 --> 00:18:34.852
- How dare you?
- I am a guest!

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:38.943
you face!

00:18:38.986 --> 00:18:40.423
You, madam,

00:18:40.466 --> 00:18:42.207
have crossed the line.

00:18:42.251 --> 00:18:44.644
...endangered my ship,
ruined my plans!

00:18:44.688 --> 00:18:46.168
Oh, I hope a temporal anomaly

00:18:46.211 --> 00:18:48.431
wipes out any record
of your existence!

00:18:48.474 --> 00:18:52.304
I've never been treated
like this in my entire life.

00:18:52.348 --> 00:18:56.003
And now I am going
to my quarters!

00:18:58.180 --> 00:19:00.921
Ransom, T'Ana, Shaxs,
you're with me.

00:19:00.965 --> 00:19:03.794
We can still get to our party.

00:19:07.014 --> 00:19:09.800
All right, who's drinking?

00:19:09.843 --> 00:19:11.541
Hey, cheer up.

00:19:11.584 --> 00:19:14.239
They've been running that
stupid party for generations.

00:19:14.283 --> 00:19:16.372
You're not the first two

00:19:16.415 --> 00:19:19.288
- to end up in here
after striking out.
- Oh, yeah?

00:19:20.767 --> 00:19:24.249
- What is that? No way.
- What?

00:19:24.293 --> 00:19:27.252
Captain Kirk drank here?

00:19:27.296 --> 00:19:30.342
He and his pointy-eared pal
tried to party-crash

00:19:30.386 --> 00:19:32.518
back in, uh, what was it?

00:19:32.562 --> 00:19:34.477
2260-something.

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:37.262
Ended up right here.

00:19:37.306 --> 00:19:39.525
Lady, you do not look that old.

00:19:39.569 --> 00:19:41.745
I am very jealous. Respect.

00:19:41.788 --> 00:19:45.009
Appreciate that, baby.

00:19:45.052 --> 00:19:47.881
Kirk and Spock drank here?
Kirk and Spock?

00:19:47.925 --> 00:19:49.840
The blond one
did most of the drinking.

00:19:49.883 --> 00:19:51.363
This is amazing.

00:19:51.407 --> 00:19:53.626
This bar's, like, history.

00:19:57.369 --> 00:19:58.588
We're here
for the captain's party.

00:19:58.631 --> 00:20:00.329
We didn't miss it, did we?

00:20:00.372 --> 00:20:02.287
Nope, they go all night long.

00:20:02.331 --> 00:20:04.289
- Yeah!
- Boom!
- Hold on.

00:20:04.333 --> 00:20:06.596
- Oh, they're with me.
- And you are?

00:20:06.639 --> 00:20:09.251
Captain Carol Freeman.

00:20:09.294 --> 00:20:11.165
Of the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:11.209 --> 00:20:13.080
- You're not on the list.

00:20:13.124 --> 00:20:15.605
I fought alongside the &lt;i&gt;Titan
at the Battle of Kallah.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:15.648 --> 00:20:17.389
Kudos. You aren't getting in.

00:20:19.696 --> 00:20:21.480
John! Captain Anderson!

00:20:21.524 --> 00:20:23.656
Could you tell him
I'm the Pakled captain?

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:25.789
Okona. How are you?

00:20:25.832 --> 00:20:28.313
Anderson! Okona is in there?

00:20:28.357 --> 00:20:29.445
He's the DJ.

00:20:29.488 --> 00:20:31.185
What? He's not even Starfleet.

00:20:31.229 --> 00:20:33.362
- This is outrageous.
- Maybe we should go.

00:20:33.405 --> 00:20:35.494
Our ship
might not be the biggest,

00:20:35.538 --> 00:20:38.758
and we might do
the missions nobody else wants,

00:20:38.802 --> 00:20:41.108
but we are still Starfleet.

00:20:41.152 --> 00:20:43.067
My crew deals
with just as much

00:20:43.110 --> 00:20:44.677
as Picard's or any other.

00:20:44.721 --> 00:20:46.244
We might be California-class,

00:20:46.288 --> 00:20:48.246
but we are the best
at what we do.

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:51.815
I'm Captain Carol Freeman,
this is my crew,

00:20:51.858 --> 00:20:54.948
and you are letting us
into that party!

00:20:56.385 --> 00:20:58.169
- I liked your speech, Captain.

00:20:58.212 --> 00:20:59.997
Thank you, Jack.

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:01.607
Hey, check it out.

00:21:01.651 --> 00:21:03.435
Should we hide?

00:21:03.479 --> 00:21:06.220
I deserve more respect.
I once escorted the &lt;i&gt;Enterprise&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:06.264 --> 00:21:09.006
- out of Spacedock, damn it.
- Oh, I hear you.

00:21:09.049 --> 00:21:12.966
One time, I let Admiral Verma
put a up my

00:21:13.010 --> 00:21:15.447
Hey, guys.
You bail on that big party?

00:21:15.491 --> 00:21:17.362
Uh, yeah. That's right.

00:21:17.406 --> 00:21:20.104
It was fine. Just, you know,
too loud in there.

00:21:20.147 --> 00:21:22.454
Oh, cool. Uh, well,
if you're not partied out,

00:21:22.498 --> 00:21:24.369
we're drinking
at Kirk's old bar.

00:21:24.413 --> 00:21:25.544
You want to check it out?

00:21:26.545 --> 00:21:28.678
Excuse me, Captain Freeman?

00:21:28.721 --> 00:21:30.549
Thank you for de-duplicating me.

00:21:30.593 --> 00:21:32.899
I really need to work
on my confidence.

00:21:32.943 --> 00:21:34.248
Yeah, you do.

00:21:34.292 --> 00:21:35.902
My meeting doesn't start
for another hour.

00:21:35.946 --> 00:21:37.469
I'm wondering if you know
any place I could relax.

00:21:37.513 --> 00:21:39.297
You know, someplace calm.

00:21:39.341 --> 00:21:42.039
You know what? I do.

00:21:42.082 --> 00:21:44.998
Captain to Transporter Room Two.

00:21:48.915 --> 00:21:52.615
Excuse me?
This is a private party.

00:21:52.658 --> 00:21:55.531
Oh! Oh, I'm so sorry.

00:22:00.362 --> 00:22:01.885
&lt;i&gt;I can't believe&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:01.928 --> 00:22:04.409
I almost got crushed
competing with myself.

00:22:04.453 --> 00:22:05.845
Well,
since you're a new Rutherford,

00:22:05.889 --> 00:22:08.370
I figured it was time
for a new model.

00:22:08.413 --> 00:22:11.982
Ooh, it comes
with an Ezri &lt;i&gt;and&lt;/i&gt; a Jadzia.

00:22:12.025 --> 00:22:15.202
- Thanks, Tendi.
- Let's never finish this one.

00:22:17.422 --> 00:22:19.642
You know what?
This worked out pretty well.

00:22:19.685 --> 00:22:23.036
Everyone I actually like
to socialize with is here.

00:22:23.080 --> 00:22:26.083
Yeah, turns out this is
the best party in the quadrant.

00:22:26.126 --> 00:22:27.693
Right, Number One?

00:22:27.737 --> 00:22:29.391
Right. Hey.

00:22:29.434 --> 00:22:31.349
No, too late.
You're my number one now.

00:22:31.393 --> 00:22:32.742
It doesn't work like that.

00:22:32.785 --> 00:22:34.439
Yes, it does.
I watched it happen.

00:22:34.483 --> 00:22:36.267
No, Captain, don't do that.
I want a redo.

00:22:36.310 --> 00:22:38.400
- No, you're my sidekick
from now on.
- I am not.

00:22:38.443 --> 00:22:41.446
Boimler's my number one!
Now he has to grow a beard.

00:23:49.296 --> 00:23:49.645
Chirp.
